WEBVTT

00:14.010 --> 00:16.320
Is this all they've got 
that's worth anything?

00:16.320 --> 00:18.910
Yeah, pretty slim pickings.

00:18.910 --> 00:20.980
They don't got enough food for us all.

00:22.850 --> 00:25.770
Guess we'll see what 
Morteln's got to plunder.

00:34.510 --> 00:36.790
Make sure you get those 
stakes in nice and deep!

00:36.790 --> 00:37.440
Sir!

00:37.440 --> 00:38.470
Boss.

00:39.020 --> 00:40.900
Looks like bad news.

00:41.690 --> 00:47.190
A village in the knight's fief of Liptaver 
was attacked and razed by bandits.

00:48.150 --> 00:50.890
It's only been three weeks since 
we returned from the capital.

00:50.890 --> 00:52.490
They've already made it to Liptaver?

00:52.890 --> 00:56.110
So they'll arrive before our 
planned two-month deadline.

00:56.110 --> 00:58.190
I'd say you're right about that.

00:58.580 --> 01:00.580
Pas. Take a message.

01:01.080 --> 01:03.840
We need the leader of each 
village here on the double.

01:03.840 --> 01:04.800
Sir!

01:04.800 --> 01:08.210
Tell Cointreau and Glacage to come as well.

01:08.520 --> 01:09.650
I will!

01:10.050 --> 01:12.490
<i>The bandits will be arriving 
sooner than expected.</i>

01:12.980 --> 01:15.240
<i>I have to stop them!</i>

01:15.710 --> 01:18.330
<i>My dream is to create a land of sweets.</i>

01:18.330 --> 01:20.550
<i>I can't let bandits destroy that dream!</i>

01:23.270 --> 01:28.270
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

01:28.270 --> 01:32.520
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

01:32.520 --> 01:35.730
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

01:36.550 --> 01:41.310
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

01:42.670 --> 01:49.140
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

01:57.050 --> 01:59.640
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

03:21.470 --> 03:25.720
<b>The Patissier and the Fief's Defense Line</b>

03:23.430 --> 03:25.930
<i>Father evaluated the situation 
and acted quickly.</i>

03:26.490 --> 03:29.330
<i>We would temporarily seal up 
the two smaller villages.</i>

03:29.660 --> 03:33.310
<i>He ordered their wells filled in, and 
their fields and homesteads stripped.</i>

03:34.380 --> 03:37.080
<i>The people from the sealed villages 
moved here to the main one.</i>

03:37.080 --> 03:39.110
<i>We'd be luring the bandits there.</i>

03:39.580 --> 03:41.970
<i>The goal was to avoid sporadic fighting.</i>

03:42.450 --> 03:43.910
Boss!

03:44.870 --> 03:47.620
I rounded up as many folks as I could.

03:48.200 --> 03:50.600
How long do you reckon we can hold out?

03:50.600 --> 03:52.190
Three days, I'd say.

03:52.190 --> 03:54.360
Though if we ration ourselves 
to one meal a day,

03:54.360 --> 03:56.750
we could stretch it out to seven.

04:01.700 --> 04:03.540
<i>We're short on forces.</i>

04:04.650 --> 04:09.600
<i>Aside from Father and his retainers 
Feuille, Cointreau, and Glacage,</i>

04:09.600 --> 04:11.060
<i>they're all peasant conscripts.</i>

04:11.560 --> 04:14.470
<i>In a prolonged campaign, we'll 
eventually be overwhelmed.</i>

04:14.470 --> 04:17.520
<i>Father and Feuille have to know that too.</i>

04:18.260 --> 04:20.180
<i>We need a plan.</i>

04:20.180 --> 04:21.990
Lord Pas!

04:21.990 --> 04:23.700
Marc! Lumi!

04:23.700 --> 04:25.200
We'll help too!

04:25.200 --> 04:28.580
We're your lieutenants, after all!

04:28.580 --> 04:29.910
My lieutenants?

04:29.910 --> 04:33.690
Our fathers are retainers to 
this land's suzerain, right?

04:33.690 --> 04:39.420
Which makes us retainers 
to its next suzerain: you!

04:40.710 --> 04:43.610
Getting the noble treatment from my two 
childhood friends makes my skin crawl.

04:43.610 --> 04:45.880
I wish you'd knock it off.

04:47.850 --> 04:51.780
<i>Normally, around this time, I'd be 
playing with them and the other kids—</i>

04:52.910 --> 04:54.550
Pas? What's up?

04:54.550 --> 04:57.220
There's a favor I'd like to ask you guys.

04:57.220 --> 04:59.570
Sure, you name it!

04:59.570 --> 05:01.560
Could you gather up rocks?

05:01.560 --> 05:02.320
Rocks?

05:02.320 --> 05:06.940
Yes. Nothing special, just the
 right size for throwing.

05:06.940 --> 05:07.780
Got it!

05:08.280 --> 05:11.660
The bandits are within the fief's 
boundaries already, right?

05:12.050 --> 05:15.540
If you hear any distant sounds 
or see anything out of the ordinary,

05:15.540 --> 05:18.500
get yourselves inside the walls 
before checking any further.

05:18.500 --> 05:20.350
As you command, Lord Pas!

05:20.350 --> 05:22.770
I told you, no noble treatment!

05:29.290 --> 05:30.720
My back's killing me!

05:31.180 --> 05:32.890
You sound like such an old man!

05:32.890 --> 05:34.330
Whaddya want from me?

05:34.330 --> 05:37.190
We've done ten laps around 
the village by now...

05:37.190 --> 05:40.900
By the way, what kind of magic 
did Pas end up with?

05:40.900 --> 05:42.230
I dunno.

05:42.230 --> 05:44.870
He says he's still practicing 
and won't tell me what it is.

05:44.870 --> 05:47.120
It's still pretty awesome.

05:47.120 --> 05:49.230
He's gotten even further ahead of you now.

05:49.230 --> 05:51.120
Whaddya mean, "even further"?!

05:51.120 --> 05:54.340
I'm still way better than him in a brawl!

05:54.340 --> 05:55.390
Yeah, yeah.

05:55.390 --> 05:58.310
Just you watch! 
I'll pound those lousy bandits—

05:59.910 --> 06:02.110
Hey, you hear something just now?

06:02.110 --> 06:02.940
Huh?

06:02.940 --> 06:06.130
No way. Your ears are just defective.

06:15.250 --> 06:16.470
Crap...

06:23.720 --> 06:25.320
They're here!

06:25.320 --> 06:26.810
The bandits!

06:26.810 --> 06:28.280
The bandits are here!

06:28.670 --> 06:29.890
Close the gate!

06:29.890 --> 06:31.570
Draw back the bridge!

06:31.570 --> 06:33.550
Don't let the bandits inside!

06:33.550 --> 06:34.700
Dad!

06:35.080 --> 06:37.750
Both of you, stay with Lord Pas.

06:37.750 --> 06:38.660
Yes, sir!

06:41.160 --> 06:44.500
Mother, get the little 
children inside at once!

06:44.500 --> 06:47.730
A-Are the bandits... really here?

06:47.730 --> 06:50.080
You really think we'll 
be enough to stop them?

06:50.820 --> 06:52.900
Stay strong, everyone!

06:54.740 --> 06:56.090
It's the suzerain lord!

06:57.680 --> 06:59.310
Listen well, everyone!

06:59.690 --> 07:01.260
If the bandits make it in here,

07:01.260 --> 07:05.770
they'll kill our people, steal our food, 
and burn our houses down!

07:05.770 --> 07:08.180
I refuse to let that happen!

07:08.180 --> 07:10.490
I ask for a similar dedication from you!

07:10.830 --> 07:13.030
Let all who share this desire 
to protect our families

07:13.030 --> 07:16.600
band together to drive these bandits back!

07:17.200 --> 07:20.300
There's not a single man here 
I believe to be a coward.

07:20.300 --> 07:21.920
I ask you to share my faith!

07:22.330 --> 07:24.500
Are you ready to do this?!

07:26.750 --> 07:28.390
<i>That's the father I know!</i>

07:28.800 --> 07:31.580
<i>The villagers were so hesitant, 
but he's filled them with courage!</i>

07:34.930 --> 07:36.980
The night will come soon.

07:36.980 --> 07:38.940
That's when the bandits will strike!

07:38.940 --> 07:40.350
Show me your spirit!

07:42.310 --> 07:44.140
Cointreau, to the western canal.

07:44.140 --> 07:44.910
Sir!

07:45.190 --> 07:48.020
Glacage, the east-to-center region.

07:48.020 --> 07:48.980
I'll handle it, sir.

07:48.980 --> 07:50.480
With me, everyone!

07:51.610 --> 07:52.450
Boss.

07:52.800 --> 07:55.430
The bandits don't know the area like we do.

07:55.430 --> 07:57.380
They'll be at a disadvantage in the dark.

07:57.810 --> 08:01.800
Don't you think they might 
wait and strike at dawn?

08:02.540 --> 08:07.050
No, I suspect they're running 
low on food and provisions.

08:07.050 --> 08:12.770
Last year's frost will have left our 
neighboring fiefs with poor crop yields.

08:13.200 --> 08:15.710
They'll want to strike as soon as possible.

08:15.710 --> 08:18.720
They'll attack at night, even if
 it's to their disadvantage.

08:18.720 --> 08:20.750
But if they don't,

08:20.750 --> 08:24.770
keeping the men up all night 
will just wear them down!

08:24.770 --> 08:26.190
What do you think, Pas?

08:27.270 --> 08:29.110
There's too much we don't know.

08:29.110 --> 08:34.660
I think we need to learn, in detail, 
the extent of the enemy's supplies and forces.

08:36.200 --> 08:37.870
<i>It's the same when making sweets.</i>

08:37.870 --> 08:40.500
<i>Before you work, you have to 
know exactly what you need</i>

08:40.500 --> 08:44.540
<i>in terms of ingredients, time, 
temperature, and everything.</i>

08:45.010 --> 08:47.990
<i>Early on, when I was making 
my first chocolate gâteau—</i>

08:48.620 --> 08:51.130
<i>No, stop that! You've got 
bigger things to focus on!</i>

08:51.130 --> 08:51.990
All right.

08:52.760 --> 08:54.350
Where are you going, Father?

08:54.350 --> 08:56.360
Aggressive reconnaissance.

08:56.360 --> 08:58.360
You'll join me, Feuille.

08:58.360 --> 09:01.320
It's still early enough for a hit-and-run.

09:01.320 --> 09:05.020
Sheesh. You're such a taskmaster, boss.

09:05.020 --> 09:08.380
Pas, you're in charge while I'm gone.

09:08.380 --> 09:09.480
Yes, sir!

09:11.690 --> 09:14.030
We'll hit the bandits hard and withdraw,

09:14.030 --> 09:18.370
taking a long detour to return 
through the northern entrance.

09:18.840 --> 09:20.030
Take care, Father!

09:20.610 --> 09:24.660
<i>I have to do what I can on my own 
before they make it back.</i>

09:26.380 --> 09:27.530
Marc.

09:27.530 --> 09:31.060
Pass a message to Cointreau 
at the western canal.

09:31.060 --> 09:33.800
"We'll use flaming arrows to 
signal the enemy's arrival."

09:34.240 --> 09:38.010
Lumi, tell Glacage to start 
preparing the flaming arrows.

09:38.990 --> 09:40.910
Tell him, once Father and 
Feuille are out of sight,

09:40.910 --> 09:44.470
the minute you hear even 
the faintest of hoofbeats again,

09:44.470 --> 09:47.130
fire the flaming arrows 
in the direction of the sound.

09:48.280 --> 09:49.520
You sure about that?

09:49.520 --> 09:52.400
The arrows could hit His Lordship as well.

09:52.400 --> 09:56.780
You think <i>my</i> father would let himself get hit 
by a stray arrow fired from that far away?

09:57.670 --> 09:59.410
Yeah, pretty hard to imagine!

10:00.050 --> 10:02.370
I mean, he showed me something 
I've never seen before...

10:04.750 --> 10:06.790
He dodged a falling rock!

10:06.790 --> 10:10.360
Yeah! He really took us to task after that.

10:10.360 --> 10:12.970
He took your dad to task for it, too!

10:14.940 --> 10:17.000
Although Father and Feuille 
know the land well,

10:17.000 --> 10:21.400
a night pursuit by bandits could 
distort their sense of direction.

10:21.400 --> 10:23.720
The flaming arrows should 
help to guide them home.

10:24.100 --> 10:26.660
Why can't he just teleport out 
with his magic?

10:26.660 --> 10:29.560
His teleportation spell has a weight limit.

10:29.560 --> 10:33.190
It would be hard for him to use it on himself, 
Feuille, and the horses all at once.

10:33.190 --> 10:35.810
Oh, really? Got it!

10:35.810 --> 10:37.400
Now, to your tasks!

10:37.400 --> 10:38.300
Right!

10:40.810 --> 10:42.230
I'm scared!

10:43.220 --> 10:45.340
What's gonna happen to the village?

10:45.340 --> 10:47.620
Hey, don't be scared. It'll be all right.

10:48.040 --> 10:53.000
My father and your fathers 
will keep us all safe.

10:53.000 --> 10:54.450
That's right.

10:54.450 --> 10:56.920
Now, Josie. Inside with you, too.

10:57.580 --> 10:58.620
Let's go.

10:59.180 --> 11:00.160
Pas.

11:02.640 --> 11:03.850
Take care.

11:03.850 --> 11:04.670
Yes, ma'am!

11:05.610 --> 11:09.020
<i>I thought sweets were the only thing 
I'd ever have to think about.</i>

11:09.640 --> 11:13.460
<i>But in this world, the only way to make 
my dream come true is to protect our fief.</i>

11:13.460 --> 11:15.730
<i>And I </i>will<i> make it come true!</i>

11:16.230 --> 11:19.040
<i>To protect these people, 
and bring smiles to their faces—</i>

11:19.040 --> 11:20.200
<i>That's what my dream means.</i>

11:20.950 --> 11:22.990
<i>That's what a land of sweets means!</i>

11:26.710 --> 11:30.070
<i>Father wants to get 
the battle over with tonight,</i>

11:30.070 --> 11:32.700
<i>even if he has to play decoy to do it.</i>

11:34.270 --> 11:36.820
<i>You're in charge while I'm gone.</i>

11:40.260 --> 11:42.690
Prepare to meet the bandits!

11:44.670 --> 11:47.620
Gather all the boys here!

12:10.390 --> 12:12.790
Boss, we've got bad news here.

12:13.830 --> 12:18.000
Our "bandits" are a gang of ex-cavalry.

12:18.650 --> 12:22.430
They've got five horses. 
Nice, able ones, at that.

12:22.430 --> 12:25.180
And they seem to know how to ride them.

12:25.180 --> 12:26.990
How many of the bandits are there?

12:27.340 --> 12:30.690
Fifty? Six—no, seventy.

12:30.690 --> 12:34.590
I doubt they were forced 
into banditry by starvation.

12:35.360 --> 12:39.220
This is likely a group of professionals.

12:39.220 --> 12:40.400
And...

12:40.810 --> 12:43.750
I see some captured villagers from somewhere.

12:43.750 --> 12:47.120
Probably being used as slaves.

12:47.660 --> 12:51.790
I'll never let them do that 
to our families and comrades!

12:51.790 --> 12:53.760
Don't fall behind, Feuille.

12:53.760 --> 12:55.500
Who do you think you're talking to?

12:55.500 --> 12:56.590
I'm more worried about you.

12:56.590 --> 13:00.090
Ride fast so you don't get 
an arrow in the butt, boss!

13:06.510 --> 13:10.390
Chief, no sign of life 
in the surrounding villages.

13:10.390 --> 13:12.560
The wells are useless. All filled in.

13:13.150 --> 13:15.340
Yeah, I figured.

13:15.760 --> 13:19.580
They've sealed the other villages 
to focus their forces in one place.

13:20.280 --> 13:22.030
Now...

13:22.380 --> 13:24.270
The sun's down.

13:24.270 --> 13:25.410
Let's head out.

13:25.410 --> 13:26.280
Right!

13:38.990 --> 13:41.050
Soldiers from Morteln?

13:47.070 --> 13:50.730
<i>They're not focused on killing, 
just making it through.</i>

13:51.550 --> 13:54.770
<i>That's some impressive 
cavalry tactics they've got...</i>

13:55.330 --> 13:57.500
<i>They gotta be trained riders!</i>

13:57.500 --> 14:00.060
They'll make another pass! Be ready!

14:04.120 --> 14:06.700
Idiots! Don't get in front of their horses!

14:07.080 --> 14:08.760
They'll trample you to death!

14:09.350 --> 14:11.830
The guy gives smart orders.

14:12.850 --> 14:15.330
We won't manage another cavalry charge.

14:17.080 --> 14:18.730
Boss, we're done for!

14:18.730 --> 14:20.720
There's too damn many of 'em!

14:20.720 --> 14:24.140
All right, let's head back 
and muster our defenses!

14:25.050 --> 14:26.530
Don't let 'em escape!

14:26.530 --> 14:28.680
After 'em! Don't let 'em 
get back to the village!

14:28.680 --> 14:30.410
There's only two of 'em!

14:28.680 --> 14:30.410
Wait, damn you!

14:30.410 --> 14:32.680
We'll catch 'em and 
strip 'em of all they got!

14:33.690 --> 14:34.890
The fools!

14:36.260 --> 14:38.300
Looks like they took the bait.

14:38.690 --> 14:40.350
Let's make it back safe!

14:45.900 --> 14:48.030
S-Sir Glacage?

14:54.480 --> 14:55.310
The fire arrows!

14:55.310 --> 14:56.700
Y-Yes, sir!

15:09.510 --> 15:10.880
My lord...

15:14.330 --> 15:15.210
The signal!

15:15.210 --> 15:17.720
They're here! The bandits are coming!

15:21.840 --> 15:24.190
A fire arrow! It's coming from the village!

15:24.190 --> 15:25.710
That's Pas.

15:25.710 --> 15:28.720
He wants to do it to guide us here,

15:28.720 --> 15:32.610
but if he's comfortable telling them 
right where the village is...

15:33.070 --> 15:34.820
He must have set a trap!

15:36.360 --> 15:39.110
If we go around the east side, 
they'll ravage the fields.

15:39.110 --> 15:40.990
We'll have to go west.

15:40.990 --> 15:43.840
I don't know what he's 
got planned, but let's go!

15:45.960 --> 15:48.100
Lord Pas! Emergency!

15:49.530 --> 15:52.970
His Lordship and Sir Feuille 
are being pursued by bandits!

15:52.970 --> 15:53.840
Did you fire the arrows?

15:53.840 --> 15:55.700
Two of them already.

15:55.700 --> 15:58.280
They're heading around the west side!

16:00.910 --> 16:02.210
Prepare to fight back!

16:11.110 --> 16:13.310
We'll kill you all!

16:14.320 --> 16:15.490
Time for that detour!

16:26.840 --> 16:28.710
Fire!

16:30.390 --> 16:31.260
What the...

16:37.440 --> 16:38.670
Damn!

16:38.670 --> 16:39.720
I knew it was a trap!

16:40.460 --> 16:41.340
Next!

16:44.250 --> 16:45.580
Fire!

16:50.610 --> 16:52.420
Fire!

16:54.200 --> 16:57.570
I never thought playing with slingshots 
would come in handy like this!

16:59.230 --> 17:03.170
<i>Once Father and Feuille have made their 
run on the bandits and head back,</i>

17:03.680 --> 17:06.040
they'll want to avoid the fields 
by taking the western route.

17:06.380 --> 17:10.750
The bandits' pursuit will likely 
leave them in a straight line.

17:11.300 --> 17:14.260
The flank of that line 
will be their weak point.

17:14.580 --> 17:16.720
We'll hit them there!

17:16.720 --> 17:19.540
A-And we're having the children do this?

17:19.540 --> 17:21.290
Hey, don't be stupid!

17:21.290 --> 17:24.180
We're better with slingshots 
than any of you guys, right?

17:25.640 --> 17:27.730
We play with 'em everyday, after all.

17:27.730 --> 17:29.170
Yeah! Yeah!

17:29.170 --> 17:31.650
We can be useful too!

17:31.650 --> 17:33.400
Ego in check, kiddo.

17:34.000 --> 17:35.860
This is still just an ambush.

17:36.470 --> 17:37.650
However...

17:37.650 --> 17:41.060
If we can disrupt their formation 
and throw their line into chaos,

17:41.060 --> 17:44.730
it will allow Father and Feuille 
more freedom to move.

17:47.810 --> 17:50.170
If the children fight with us,

17:50.170 --> 17:52.730
we can make up for our 
numerical disadvantage.

17:54.010 --> 17:56.010
The minute the enemy crosses the canal,

17:56.010 --> 17:58.080
the children will fall back,

17:58.080 --> 18:00.260
and the armed villagers will meet them.

18:01.360 --> 18:02.950
All right.

18:02.950 --> 18:06.860
Our lord told us to protect 
the village together.

18:06.860 --> 18:09.540
Let's carry out Lord Pas's plan!

18:09.540 --> 18:10.730
Yeah!

18:11.100 --> 18:14.690
Yeah! Let's show those 
old guys what we can do!

18:15.340 --> 18:16.480
Lumi...

18:17.040 --> 18:18.970
I mean, you're a girl.

18:18.970 --> 18:21.350
I'd really rather you sit this one out.

18:21.350 --> 18:23.400
What the hell?

18:23.400 --> 18:25.260
I'm an exception, right?

18:25.260 --> 18:28.080
You can't tell the next lord's personal 
retainer she can't participate.

18:28.080 --> 18:31.360
I guess... yeah, thanks.

18:31.360 --> 18:33.320
I'm not sure if I can do it.

18:38.030 --> 18:39.320
Lord Pas...

18:39.320 --> 18:41.250
It's okay. You can do it.

18:41.580 --> 18:44.090
Just treat it like you're 
playing, like always.

18:44.960 --> 18:45.970
Yes, sir!

18:46.670 --> 18:50.040
<i>I won't let the children get hurt!</i>

18:50.040 --> 18:51.510
Fire!

18:55.460 --> 18:57.210
Nice work, kid!

18:57.210 --> 18:59.000
Let's go, Feuille! Keep it up!

18:59.000 --> 19:00.790
You got it, Boss!

19:01.950 --> 19:04.000
Damn kids...

19:09.150 --> 19:11.040
One's heading our way!

19:11.040 --> 19:12.500
Fire!

19:16.640 --> 19:17.710
No more games!

19:29.110 --> 19:31.560
Follow the chief!

19:32.780 --> 19:34.270
Th-They're here!

19:36.770 --> 19:38.790
Lord Pas, run!

19:54.320 --> 19:57.270
If you wanna die, come try me!

20:02.560 --> 20:04.360
Your opponents are right here.

20:06.780 --> 20:07.790
Bring it on!

20:14.780 --> 20:18.280
Boss, their leader went after the kids!

20:22.450 --> 20:25.410
It's hot! It's hot!

20:32.850 --> 20:36.140
I've had enough of your games!

20:43.180 --> 20:44.520
Lord Pas!

20:44.520 --> 20:46.390
Get the children inside.

20:46.870 --> 20:48.240
Lord Pas!

20:48.240 --> 20:49.600
Don't you move!

20:50.670 --> 20:51.710
Lord Pas!

20:53.720 --> 20:55.270
Don't you move.

20:55.660 --> 20:57.270
A coward's trick.

21:02.170 --> 21:03.460
<i>That man...</i>

21:04.000 --> 21:05.360
<i>I can use him!</i>

21:05.900 --> 21:08.370
C'mon, you bastards! Get 'em!

21:12.610 --> 21:13.750
<i>Replicate!</i>

21:20.350 --> 21:21.880
Wh-What the...

21:30.310 --> 21:35.730
My face... My face is on fire!

21:38.970 --> 21:42.350
D-Damn you... What'd you do to me?!

21:42.840 --> 21:44.570
Nothing much.

21:45.630 --> 21:48.070
I merely replicated your comrade's wound.

21:49.150 --> 21:51.870
R-Replicated?

21:52.610 --> 21:53.870
Can it be—

21:54.310 --> 21:56.080
You're a...

21:56.080 --> 21:58.550
magic... user?

21:59.510 --> 22:00.570
No.

22:01.090 --> 22:03.020
I'm just a patissier.

23:37.160 --> 23:39.110
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.020 --> 23:44.980
<b>Apple Pie and Smiles</b>

23:39.440 --> 23:41.830
"Apple Pie and Smiles."

23:41.830 --> 23:43.240
Bon appétit!

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
<b>Seriko Iida</b>
